WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:06.160
The second Fantastic Beasts film brings together
the story of Newt Scamander and his old professor

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.420
Albus Dumbledore.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.820
Throughout, fans can find a ton of Easter
eggs hidden throughout the picture that only

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.400
the truest Harry Potter aficionados are bound
to catch.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.540
Pull out your wand, and get your anti-spoiler
spell ready: here are the small details you

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.860
missed in Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of
Grindelwald.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.120
In The Crimes of Grindelwald, there's a lot
to unpack about the relationship between the

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.700
titular villain and his opposite-equal, Albus
Dumbledore.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.700
Dumbledore's visit to the Mirror of Erised
does help reveal some of the major points:

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:41.040
In it, he sees his younger self making a blood
pact with the boy he says he was "closer than

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:41.580
brothers" with.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.140
Not only does that call back a similar scene
from Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.680
when the Boy Wizard summons up a happier image
of his parents, it also earns a more subtle

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.620
bit of nostalgia from the original series
thanks to who we see in it.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:59.620
Actors Toby Regbo and Jamie Campbell Bower
reprise their roles as Dumbledore and Grindelwald

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.700
in Fantastic Beasts 2, after having portrayed
the characters ever so briefly in Harry Potter

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.740
and the Deathly Hallows: Part 1.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.220
Considering how small their screen time was
in the original series, they could've easily

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.940
been replaced, but seeing them return to these
roles nicely bridges the gap between the film

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:16.480
sets.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:21.680
The sweeping new shots of an unfettered Hogwarts
probably made for a very welcome sight for

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.540
Harry Potter fans who cringed with every artifact's
destruction in the Second Wizarding War in

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.400
Deathly Hallows: Part 2.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.360
The bridge is shown intact, the Great Hall
is perfectly lit by floating candles, and,

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.340
of course, Dumbledore's office is still filled
with so many of his intriguing tools of the

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:37.860
trade.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:42.600
The scenes involving young Dumbledore also
featured a few namedrops that will ring familiar

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:43.280
to fans.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:48.020
First, there's the instruction for the students
to go with Professor McGonagall, who we all

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.580
know and love so well from the Harry Potter
series.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.350
Then, one student's name is called out as
Mclaggen, who must be the ancestor of this

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.060
Gryffindor student from the original series,
Cormac McLaggen.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.310
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald
also turned what we knew about an old Harry

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:08.940
Potter character on its head when it revealed
that Nagini was not always the snake sidekick

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:09.740
of the Dark Lord.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:15.420
Instead, she was formerly a person with the
Maledictus curse, which meant that she shape-shifted

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.580
into snake form and one day would not be able
to change back.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.680
There's a running theory that she might turn
out to be Tom Riddle's actual mother before

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.940
it's all said and done.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:28.340
It would certainly help explain the allegiance
she develops for the character later on — not

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:33.080
to mention his eventual snakey features and
his gift with parseltongue — especially

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.380
if she were to, say, conceive Voldemort with
Credence.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:41.180
On the other hand, the books and films have
already established Riddle's parentage, so

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:45.180
if the Fantastic Beasts films decide to go
a different direction, they'll have a whole

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.540
lot of explaining to do.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:52.340
Harry Potter fans may have previously only
known of Nicholas Flamel thanks to Harry,

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:57.629
Hermione, and Ron discovering how he created
the Philosopher's Stone and achieved immortality

00:02:57.629 --> 00:03:01.239
— or at least really, really long life — in
the first installment.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.400
However, Fantastic Beasts 2 gives us a fuller
glimpse of the character in his crone-like

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.900
decrepit form — as well as a quick glimpse
of that elusive Philospher's Stone in Flamel's

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:11.440
house.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.800
But unlike most of Rowling's characters, Flamel
was actually a real person, and was rumored

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.820
to have used alchemy to become immortal.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.240
"Nickola Flamel.”

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.360
“Jacob Kowalski.”

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:22.840
“Oh!”

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.540
"You don’t look a day over 375.”

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:31.319
The end of Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of
Grindelwald features a big twist, where we

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.200
finally learn about Credence's family history.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.440
After narrowly escaping capture in the first
film, he spends this movie trying to track

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.680
down the identity of his real parents and
figure out why they decided to leave him in

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.940
the care of a horrible woman like Mary Lou
Barebone.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:50.880
In the end, he discovers that he isn't the
long-lost sibling of Leta LeStrange, as he'd

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:55.480
expected, but that he was actually named Aurelius
Dumbledore — and that Albus Dumbledore is

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:58.120
trying to destroy him, according to Grindelwald.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.620
If there's one thing these Wizarding World
stories love, it's family drama, and the revelation

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:07.500
that Credence could actually be related to
Dumbledore is the good stuff.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.060
Fans of the franchise are probably poring
over their books to see if they can figure

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:15.360
out where this new information fits into the
ever-expanding Harry Potter universe.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:20.580
If only hearing the actors say the name "Dumbledore"
with such gravitas didn't sound quite so,

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.560
well…

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:22.740
"Ridikkulus."

